# `xrandr --output HEADLESS-1 --scale 2x2`, measured 2026-09-10 (cap1.log
# connection 10, requests 19-23): grab, disable, SetScreenSize(2560x1440),
# SetCrtcTransform, enable. No ungrab -- Xwayland answered the transform
# BadValue (minor 26, value 0x20 [recon/env.md 2.4]) and xrandr died.
#
# The transform is the whole reason this request is decoded rather than passed:
# `--scale 2x2` sends exactly [[2,0,0],[0,2,0],[0,0,1]] in 16.16 fixed point
# plus the filter name `bilinear`, and that is a scale every output-management
# protocol carries. Anything with a shear or a translation in it is not, and
# answers BadValue -- the same byte Xwayland answers for all of them today.
24000100
